// How near a vehicle of examples/parking is to walls, a point at its
// rounded corner and a kerb placed at distances known by hand
// (check/clear.ent; parking-SPEC.md, check 2), in tenths of a
// millimetre, and one that drives at a wall, which stops short of it.
// On one core and on all.
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/../../examples/parking %S/../../examples/parking/check/clear.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel -I %S/../../examples/parking %S/../../examples/parking/check/clear.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.one

// A tall wall: the mirror. A low one: the body, under the mirror.
// CHECK: car 0 gap 4560 edge 0
// CHECK: car 1 gap 5755 edge 1
// CHECK: car 2 gap 3000 edge 2
// The rounded corner.
// CHECK: car 3 gap 4278 edge 3
// A kerb is the tyres' alone.
// CHECK: car 4 gap {{[0-9]+}} edge 5 kerb 500 hits 0
// CHECK: car 5 gap 2500 edge 5
// CHECK: car 6 gap 10000 edge 6
// After 5 s at the wall.
// CHECK: car 5 gap 2500 edge 5 kerb {{[0-9]+}} hits 0 stopped false
// CHECK: car 6 gap {{[0-9]+}} edge 6 kerb {{[0-9]+}} hits {{[1-9]}} stopped true within true v 0.0
